# Data Warehouse Modeling and Architecture Standards

## Star Schema Implementation
- MUST implement proper star schema with fact and dimension tables
- MUST use surrogate keys for all dimension tables (sk_table_name pattern)
- MUST implement slowly changing dimensions (SCD Type 2) for historical tracking
- MUST use appropriate data types for optimal storage and query performance
- MUST implement proper indexing strategies for large fact tables

## Fact Table Design
- MUST use grain-appropriate fact tables (transaction-level for orders)
- MUST implement proper foreign key relationships to dimension tables
- MUST use appropriate partitioning strategies (date, region, product category)
- MUST implement data compression for storage optimization
- MUST ensure referential integrity between fact and dimension tables

## Dimension Table Design
- MUST implement conformed dimensions for consistent business logic
- MUST use proper surrogate keys with auto-incrementing integers
- MUST implement SCD Type 2 for slowly changing attributes
- MUST include effective date ranges for historical tracking
- MUST implement proper data validation and cleansing

## Data Partitioning Strategy
- MUST partition large fact tables by date (daily partitions recommended)
- MUST implement multi-level partitioning for complex queries
- MUST use appropriate partition sizes (100MB-1GB recommended)
- MUST implement partition pruning for query optimization
- MUST use partition discovery for efficient data reading

## Performance Optimization
- MUST implement proper indexing on frequently queried columns
- MUST use columnar storage formats (Parquet) with compression
- MUST implement data compression for storage and I/O optimization
- MUST use appropriate file formats for different use cases
- MUST implement data compaction for small files

## Data Quality and Governance
- MUST implement data quality checks at ETL pipeline stages
- MUST validate referential integrity between related tables
- MUST implement data lineage tracking for compliance
- MUST document data definitions and business rules
- MUST implement data retention policies

## Scalability Considerations
- MUST design for horizontal scaling of data volumes
- MUST implement proper resource allocation for large queries
- MUST use appropriate cluster sizing for expected workloads
- MUST implement query optimization for concurrent users
- MUST plan for data growth and performance requirements

## Testing and Validation
- MUST implement unit tests for data transformations
- MUST validate data quality metrics and thresholds
- MUST test query performance with realistic data volumes
- MUST implement regression testing for schema changes
- MUST validate data consistency across related tables